# API Layer Integration - Endpoint Map Template

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "REST API"
        GET_U[GET /users]
        POST_U[POST /users]
        GET_U_ID[GET /users/{id}]
        PUT_U_ID[PUT /users/{id}]
        DEL_U_ID[DELETE /users/{id}]
    end
    
    subgraph "GraphQL"
        GQL_Query[Query: users, user]
        GQL_Mutation[Mutation: createUser, updateUser]
        GQL_Subscription[Subscription: userUpdated]
    end
    
    subgraph "gRPC"
        GRPC_UserSvc[UserService]
        GRPC_GetUser[GetUser]
        GRPC_ListUsers[ListUsers]
        GRPC_CreateUser[CreateUser]
        GRPC_UpdateUser[UpdateUser]
    end
    
    subgraph "Async / Events"
        Kafka_UserCreated[user.created]
        Kafka_UserUpdated[user.updated]
        Kafka_UserDeleted[user.deleted]
    end
    
    style GET_U fill:#e3f2fd
    style POST_U fill:#e3f2fd
    style GQL_Query fill:#f3e5f5
    style GRPC_UserSvc fill:#e8f5e9
    style Kafka_UserCreated fill:#fff3e0
```

## Usage
Map all your API endpoints across different protocols and styles.